## What this session delivered

**Defect closed (9 → 8 OPEN):** D-DWORK-TEARDOWN-LASTREF-LEAK is FIXED AND VERIFIED — a bast-arm gate across all 25 per-inode arm sites plus a put_super s_inodes sweep that breaks the last-ref circular the workqueue flush can't see. Verified by live engagement (cancels=1, refs_dropped=1 on every teardown, ×7) with zero leak signature, and a clean board. En route: discovered `xfs_io shutdown` had been a silent no-op on mxfs forever; GOINGDOWN is now implemented (0.11.312) so shutdown fault-injection is real.

**Pace-family campaign (four RULE-4, stack-proven protocol fixes, 314–317):** direct EX grant handoff + PR-class batch grant (8.6× total grant-wait reduction in a same-build A/B, 95.8s → 11.1s), clean-PR retention across eviction, and a DLM-free eofblocks peek — together they killed the drop_caches convoy (6–9s → 0.15s). Result: **dir_reuse_coherency passed for the first time in 11 runs** (58/58, exactly at the 8-round floor — still OPEN, zero margin), and the **full 32-node board on 0.11.317 is 20/21 with zero regressions**, with fio throughput up substantially.

**Root of the remaining margin gap, proven live:** each create runs lookup-PR → EX upgrade → EDEADLK → drop+drain → fresh EX. The fix — CREATEINT (create-intent lookups take the dir at cluster-EX, mirroring the existing PRIREAD flag) — is **fully implemented and builds clean as 0.11.318** (srcversion 2E2DD3DB), but is **not deployed and not tested**; the exact verification sequence (instr-window rc=-35 count, dir_reuse ×3 targeting ≥9 rounds, full board, knob A/B fallback) is recorded.

